# `||` right before an operator is two pipes, not C's `or`: DS0103.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' || take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..28
  PIPELINE@0..27
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE2@18..20 "||"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
    TAKE_OP@21..27
      IDENT@21..25 "take"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      LITERAL@26..27
        LONG@26..27 "5"
  WHITESPACE@27..28 "\n"

error[DS0103]: two `|` in a row
  --> query:1:19
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' || take 5
  |                   ^^ one `|` is enough
  |
  = help: remove the extra `|`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | take 5
which parses without errors
